diff --git a/docs/prewarm.md b/docs/prewarm.md
index ffc931c57..935c53896 100644
--- a/docs/prewarm.md
+++ b/docs/prewarm.md
@@ -12,3 +12,14 @@ These interfaces are proposed extensions, not upstream compatibility promises.
 
 Preparation also compiles the existing virtio seccomp filters before restore.
 Workers still install their own filters before running device code.
+
+## CPU profile preparation
+
+`vmm.prepare` accepts `vcpu_ids`, consecutive IDs starting at zero (at most
+256). KVM descriptor creation happens before restore; architectural state
+initialization stays in the existing CPU restore path. Unused descriptors
+are owned by the prepared VM and dropped with it. Empty IDs retain generic prewarm only.
+
+Prepared vCPU IDs must match the actual restored boot CPU count and topology.
+A mismatch is rejected before restoring state or preparing template memory;
+unused reserved kernel vCPUs are never silently attached to a different VM.
